{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
{"@type":"Question","name":"When should an auto detailer collect payment?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For many consumer jobs, collecting the balance at completion is simpler than allowing an open-ended pay-later arrangement. Higher-ticket or high-risk jobs may justify a deposit. Your policy should be communicated before the work starts."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Should detailers require deposits?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Deposits can reduce cancellation and collection risk, especially for long or high-ticket jobs, but they can also add booking friction. Use them selectively and state refund or cancellation terms clearly."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"Can Housecall Pro take deposits and online payments?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Housecall Pro documents dollar or percentage deposits, online invoice payments, card payments, ACH and card-on-file workflows. Online Booking can also require deposits or full payment."}},
{"@type":"Question","name":"What if a customer says they will pay later?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Decide your exception policy before the situation happens. If you allow deferred payment, send the invoice immediately, document the agreed due date and follow a consistent reminder/escalation process rather than improvising."}}
]}

